menu "RoboHub STM32 Platform"

config ROBOHUB_STM32
    bool "Enable the RoboHub STM32 platform"
    default y
    help
      Implementations of the RoboHub HAL interfaces on the STM32 HAL and
      CMSIS. A project that depends on robohub-stm32 needs this; a project on
      another platform does not.

config ROBOHUB_STM32_CLOCK
    bool "Configure the clock tree during platform init"
    default y
    help
      Switch the STM32 into the clock configuration the board asks for, using
      the external oscillator the board is fitted with. Turning this off leaves
      the reset clock configuration in place, which is what a board brought up
      under a debugger wants.

config ROBOHUB_STM32_ASSERT
    bool "Check driver arguments and report failures"
    default y
    help
      Have the HAL implementations reject an invalid argument with
      ROBOHUB_ERR_INVALID_ARG rather than writing to a peripheral that was not
      configured. A driver that does not check is faster; a driver that does not
      check turns a wiring mistake into a silent wrong answer.

# The per-driver symbols live in kconfig/hal/, one fragment per interface. They
# are not sourced from here: the build passes each fragment to the generator
# explicitly, which is how robohub-common does it, and a fragment that is both
# sourced and passed would be defined twice by anything that follows sources.

endmenu
